@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFDF9
skinparam defaultFontName Tahoma
title Runtime component layers - code baseline adc5798 (8 Oct 2026)
top to bottom direction
component "React views / shared components\nCustomer / Staff / Kitchen / Manager" as Web
package "Spring Boot REST application" {
 component "Controllers\nHTTP / Bean Validation / response DTOs" as C
 component "Application services\nTable/Session: DiningSessionServiceImpl / CustomerSessionAccessService\nCatalog/Ordering: MenuCatalogServiceImpl / CustomerOrderingServiceImpl\nFulfillment: OrderFulfillmentServiceImpl / OrderStateResolver / RegistryOrderStateResolver\nBilling/Payment: BillingEngine / PaymentServiceImpl / CustomerBillingService\nAuth/Stock: AuthService / StockService / StockTransactionTemplate" as S
 component "Cross-module contracts\nSessionContextProvider\nDiningSessionBillingReader\nPaymentStatusLookup\nBillCalculator / CustomerSessionVerifier" as Contracts
 component "Session access providers\nUserContextProvider / SessionUserContextProvider\nStaff / Fulfillment / Payment / Menu" as Auth
 component "DTO mappers\nTable / DiningSession\nCatalog / Ordering" as M
 component "Spring Data JPA repositories\nEntity queries / pessimistic row locks" as Repo
 component "Domain entities\nTables / Sessions / Orders\nPayments / Users / Stock" as E
}
database "PostgreSQL\nSupabase Session Pooler + SSL" as DB
component "Flyway\ncommon + postgresql V1-V15" as Fly
Web --> C : JSON / staff login session / customer cookie
C --> S : use cases
S --> Repo : transactions / queries
Repo --> DB : JDBC
Repo --> E : JPA mapping
S ..> Contracts : provider collaboration
S --> Auth : API authorization
S --> M : public response mapping
Fly --> DB : schema version / checksum
note bottom of Contracts
 Ordering -> SessionContextProvider -> customer/session access
 Billing -> DiningSessionBillingReader -> opening-price snapshot
 Close -> PaymentStatusLookup -> same-session PAID
 Runtime: database/session. Fixtures: explicit demo/tests only.
end note
note bottom of Auth
 Shared UserSessionKeys removes the service-to-controller dependency.
 Session collaborations use verifier / reader / payment-lookup contracts.
 The inspected services use constructor injection; JPA and domain dependencies remain.
 Public deployment and Final release still require their own acceptance.
end note
@enduml
